Major Collaborative Projects
======

**International joint research on the seismic performance of full-scale steel buildings**  
Japan Society for the Promotion of Science (22KK0063), 2022-2027. Core research member responsible for test planning, instrumentation, data acquisition, response analysis, and numerical simulation for the E-Defense full-scale 10-story steel building test.

**Challenging research on the collapse behavior of multi-story steel buildings**  
Japan Society for the Promotion of Science (20K20435), 2020-2023. Core research member involved in instrumentation, data acquisition, data processing, and numerical analysis for a large-scale four-story steel frame shake-table collapse test.

**Open Research Fund of the National Center for Earthquake Engineering, Tianjin University**  
2025-2027. Core research member and third contributor.

**Industry-university collaborative research on innovative CFST structures and connections for the Pinghu Convention and Exhibition Center**  
2025-present. Major research contributor.

Selected Large-Scale Experimental Programs
======

- Full-scale 10-story steel building tested on the E-Defense three-dimensional shake table
- Large-scale four-story steel moment-resisting frame shake-table collapse test
- Full-scale steel beam-to-HSS column connection tests with composite slabs
- Full-scale curtain wall inter-story drift tests
- Large-scale cyclic tests of irregular steel beam-to-CFST column connections
